Adds four new operations to the Jira Cloud plugin:
- get_issue_properties: GET /issue/{issueIdOrKey}/properties
- get_issue_property: GET /issue/{issueIdOrKey}/properties/{propertyKey}
- set_issue_property: PUT /issue/{issueIdOrKey}/properties/{propertyKey}
- delete_issue_property: DELETE /issue/{issueIdOrKey}/properties/{propertyKey}

Also updates README.md to reflect the new capabilities.

Expand ontology coverage to include missing ROS2 nav_msgs:
- Implement OccupancyGrid, MapMetadata, Path and GridCells Ontology models;

Closes #398

Addresses https://app.plane.so/ituxakaxsyvai/browse/ITUXA-80/

## Major change

To fix the validation issue, it was necessary to change the config schema of llm judge.
A rubric that before looked like this:
```
"rubric" : [
	"correctness: Is the advice scientifically valid?",
	"clarity: Is the explanation easy to understand?"
]
```
will now look like this
```
"rubric" : [
	{ "id": "correctness", "description": "Is the advice scientifically valid?" },
	{ "id": "clarity", "description": "Is the explanation easy to understand?" },
]
```

The readme example has also been changed accordingly.

## Do this please :)
Design decisions are on the plane issue. Please have a look at the code and see if you agree with my solution. I found this to be the most robust with as little possible change to the models.

I'd also like reviewers to run a few llm judge requests. I have been using the monstrosity below to debug, so you can use that, or better yet, build your own request.

*Note: If you have old evaluation results in your database, stuff might *

