After a successful Excel restore, all four tables contained only auto-incremented IDs; every string column (`name`, `type`, `icon`, etc.) was empty and every boolean (`enable`) was `0`, despite the `.wmbak` file holding complete data.

## Root cause

`restoreAllTablesFromExcel` called Room DAO `insertXxxSync()` methods **inside** an already-open `rawDb.beginTransaction()`. Room's generated DAO code unconditionally calls `__db.beginTransaction()` on entry — this nested call interferes with the outer raw transaction on Android's SQLite layer, causing the inserts to be silently lost. The DELETEs committed fine; the INSERTs did not. Return value was still `true`.

A secondary symptom: the AUTOINCREMENT `sqlite_sequence` high-water mark was not reset after `DELETE`, so even partial inserts came back with IDs continuing from the old maximum (48, 49, …) instead of the backup's original IDs (1, 2, …).

## Changes — `ExcelBackupManager.restoreAllTablesFromExcel`

- **Replace DAO inserts with `rawDb.execSQL()`** — every `DELETE` and `INSERT OR REPLACE` now runs on the same `SupportSQLiteDatabase` connection inside the same transaction; no Room-managed nested transaction can interfere.

```java
// Before — nested Room transaction swallows the inserts
if (!categories.isEmpty()) db.categoryDetailsDao().insertCategoriesSync(categories);

// After — same connection, same transaction
for (CategoryDetails c : categories) {
    rawDb.execSQL(
        "INSERT OR REPLACE INTO category_details (id, name, type, time, enable, icon) VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?)",
        new Object[]{ c.id, c.categoryName, c.categoryType, c.time, c.enable ? 1 : 0, c.icon });
}
```

- **Reset `sqlite_sequence`** after the DELETE block so restored IDs are used as-is and subsequent inserts continue from the correct high-water mark.

```java
rawDb.execSQL("DELETE FROM sqlite_sequence WHERE name IN "
    + "('account_details','category_details','record_details','budget_details')");
```

